The Site allows the customer to create a personalised photo album from the photographs they select and upload to the platform.

Depending on the options offered on the Site, the customer may choose in particular:
• the photographs included in the album;
• their order and arrangement;
• the album format;
• the number of pages;
• the cover;
• the layout;
• texts and other customisation elements;
• and any other option offered on the Site.

The customer is responsible for checking their album before finally confirming their order, including where all or part of the selection or layout results from a suggestion generated by an artificial intelligence tool.

In particular, it is up to the customer to check the selected photographs, their orientation, framing and order, the inserted texts, spelling, the number of pages and the other customisation choices.

The digital representation of the album shown on the Site is a preview. Slight differences may exist between this preview and the printed product, notably in colours, brightness, contrast, framing or rendering, due in particular to the characteristics of screens, of the files provided and of the printing process.

Such differences are not a product defect when they remain within normal printing tolerances.

When the Site is used and orders are fulfilled, the Company may process in particular:
• the customer's identification data;
• their contact details;
• their delivery address;
• information about their orders;
• the photographs and other files they upload, including, where applicable, images of identifiable individuals or minors;
• the information needed for payment, within the limits required for the transaction.

This data is processed in accordance with the applicable Lebanese legislation, in particular Law no. 81/2018 on electronic transactions and personal data.

Uploaded photographs are used only to the extent necessary to provide the service, unless the customer expressly consents to another use.

Given the particular nature of some photographs (in particular when they show identifiable people or minors), the Company applies appropriate security and confidentiality measures. It does not use these photographs for facial recognition: automatic face detection is used only to frame photographs in the layout, without ever identifying the people shown.

Some data and photographs may be sent to the providers involved in fulfilling the order, in particular the printing house and, where necessary, the delivery provider.

These providers must only receive the information needed to carry out their tasks.

Detailed information on the collection, use, retention, sharing and deletion of personal data is given in the Privacy Policy available on the Site.

Uploaded photographs are kept according to the following rules:
• album not ordered: it is automatically deleted, with its photographs, 30 days after it was created;
• unused photographs: photographs uploaded but not included in the final layout of an ordered album are deleted once the order's print file has been generated;
• ordered album: the album, its photographs and the order history are kept for as long as the customer's account exists, to allow a reprint, to let the customer find their album again, or to handle any complaint.

The customer can delete their account at any time from their account page ("Delete my account"): their account, albums and photographs are then permanently deleted. Information about past orders (amount, delivery address) is kept for accounting purposes, without any photograph. Deletion is not possible while an order is being manufactured or delivered.

The customer may also ask for their photographs to be deleted earlier once keeping them is no longer necessary to fulfil the order or to handle an ongoing complaint, as described in the Privacy Policy.

The Company is responsible for performing its obligations in accordance with the applicable law.

However, it cannot be held liable for a defect resulting solely from:
• a photograph or file of insufficient quality provided by the customer;
• an error in text, selection, framing or layout approved by the customer, including when that error was already present in a suggestion generated by an artificial intelligence tool that the customer accepted without correcting it;
• an incorrect delivery address provided by the customer;
• use of the service contrary to these Terms or to the law;
• or a force majeure event within the meaning of the applicable law.

Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits any liability that cannot legally be excluded or limited under Lebanese law.
